<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105801" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρώκ-της</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρώγω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gnawer, mibbler</i>: but in
				<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				14.289
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				15.416
			</span></i>, Phoenician traffickers are called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῶκται,</span>
			<i>greedy knaves</i>; so 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. σφόδρ᾽ ἐστίν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Com.Adesp.</u>
					606
				</span></i>
			; and Gramm. explain <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρώκτης</span>
			by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάγος, φιλοκερδής, πανοῦργος, ἀπατεών,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				1757.51
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλοχρήματοι καὶ τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>Her.Prooem.</u>
					1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as
			Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῶκται χεῖρες</span>
			<i>greedy</i> hands, of a usurer, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.409
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphan.
			</span></i>, dub. cj.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a sea-fish with sharp teeth,</i>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμία</span>
			 (q.v.), <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				1.5
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
